    desc: 'Retrofuturism is the retrospective enjoyment of past futures: ray-gun rocketships, household robots, monorails, dome cities and atomic-age optimism as seen from after their promised dates failed to arrive. The term covers a family of styles — Atompunk\'s tailfins, Dieselpunk\'s riveted machinery, Raygun Gothic\'s swooping pulp craft — and a criticism tradition (paleofuturism) that studies why futures were imagined as they were. Designers mine it for warmth without nostalgia irony; manga and games borrow its confident chrome. The core appeal: a future that believed in itself, now viewable as period charm.',
