    desc: 'Dieselpunk is the retrofuture of the interwar years: riveted dreadnought geometry, airship hangars, testbed monoplanes, streamliner locomotives, art-deco radios and the somber industrial palette of oil, steel and smoke. The term — coined online in 2001 (Lewis Pollak & Dan LaSoura, for the RPG Children of the Sun) — sets the tone against steampunk\'s brass: diesel is grimmer, heavier, film-grainier. Games (Crimson Skies, Iron Harvest, Bioshock\'s rapture-era machines), cosplay and model-making sustain the aesthetic, and its art direction leans on Weimar posters, WPA murals and RKO serial menace.',
