    desc: 'Silkpunk is Ken Liu\'s term (The Grace of Kings, 2015) for a retrofuture built from East Asian materials and logic: bamboo, silk, paper and rope instead of iron and steam — airships that are octopus-kites, spring-driven carts, silk-string telegraphs, diving gears of lacquered hide. Where steampunk asks "what if steam won?", silkpunk asks "what if engineering followed silk and bamboo?" — yielding machines that bend, breathe and flutter. The aesthetic values tensile structure over rigidity, and its illustration tradition (Dandelion Dynasty covers, fan art) favors brushwork gradients and seagoing color. It has become a touchstone for non-Western futurism in fiction.',
