    sum: 'Spaceships with mud on the tires: dents, grease, and cobbled panels.',
    desc: '"Used future" names the science-fiction look in which spaceships are work vehicles, not miracles: the Millennium Falcon\'s worn hull, Alien\'s Nostromo break-room, blade-runner drizzle — surfaces dented, duct-taped and grease-streaked, sets dressed like long-serving machinery. The look crystallized as a rebuke to gleaming-thryptic futures (2001, Star Trek bridge gloss): modelmakers (Industrial Light & Magic), production designers (Roger Christian\'s "used universe" brief for Star Wars) and art directors built grime into hero props. Games (Outer Wilds, Hardspace: Shipbreaker) and shows (The Expanse, Andor) inherit it: the future as blue-collar workplace.',
