    sum: 'Glossy, plausible tomorrows — the concept-art language behind Blade Runner\'s spinners.',
    desc: 'Syd Mead — "visual futurist", his own coinage — defined the slick end of retrofuture: airbrushed renderings of plausible machinery, from US Steel and Philips product futures to Blade Runner\'s spinner cars, Tron light-cycle roots, Aliens\' Sulaco, and Japan\'s Sony/Sharp concept commissions. Mead\'s grammar: strong single-light staging, believable wear on optimistic surfaces, people dwarfed by elegant hardware, and a rendering polish that made the impossible look like next year\'s brochure. Concept-art education still teaches from his books (Oblagon, Sentury), and "Mead-style" remains shorthand for corporate-future glamour with grit.',
